Zero-copy display: the flush fence the host holds until its compositor
released the buffer shown before gets a dma-fence context of its own.

virtio_gpu_fence_event_process() signals, with each completed fence, every
earlier fence of the same context.  The held flush fence shared the default
context with the cursor plane's transfers and resource commands, so any of
them completing while the host held the flush signalled it early: the flip
event went out, the compositor rendered into a buffer the host still showed
(corruption of moved windows, a darker panel for a refresh).  The command
still goes out without a ring index, so the host still holds it.

diff -ru a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_display.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_display.c	2026-10-02 10:28:50.705614608 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_display.c	2026-10-02 10:29:01.310638844 +0200
@@ -672,6 +672,7 @@
 	int ret;
 
 	output->index = index;
+	output->flush_fence_context = dma_fence_context_alloc(1);
 	spin_lock_init(&output->vblank_lock);
 	hrtimer_setup(&output->vblank_timer, virtio_gpu_vblank_timer,
 		      CLOCK_MONOTONIC, HRTIMER_MODE_ABS);
